    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but some of the senior devs are pushing back. they're saying that focusing on outcomes instead of individual merit or 'equality of opportunity' might actually be seen as a form of reverse discrimination or just mathematically unsound. how would you respond to people saying that equality of opportunity is the only truly fair way to handle credit scoring?",
