      "content": "The argument for \"equality of opportunity\" is a smokescreen for maintaining the status quo that benefits the already privileged. True fairness requires correcting historical imbalances, which is precisely what equality of outcome achieves. Meritocracy, when applied to a system built on unequal starting lines, is just a sophisticated way of codifying existing inequality. We must prioritize equitable results over the flawed notion of a level playing field that doesn't exist.",
      "source": "target",
